Feature: TC_12_STAFF - Scheme Selection BISS CRISS Protein Eco MSSM RCSM E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Pack for Scheme Selection - Add BISS, CRISS" (BISSAGL-5919, AT-TC-01 to 04,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-14880 / 14879 / 14877 / 14876)
  #           "Regression Pack for Scheme Selection - Add MSSM, RCSM" (BISSAGL-7582, AT-TC-01 to 05,
  #           tmslinks BISSAGL-14893 / 14889 / 14885 / 14891 / 14890)
  # Rewritten 15-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary. Modernised 22-10-2026: one end-to-end scenario in which every
  # check runs once; # SECTION markers show which legacy scenarios each part covers.
  #
  # Flow:
  #   SECTION 1 : amendable herd / 2026 - BISS and CRISS cards: position, acronym, full name, View Details dialog, toggle
  #   SECTION 2 : same screen - CRISS and Protein Aid Scheme selected, Next, Back, deselected: nothing changes
  #   SECTION 3 : same screen - CRISS, Protein Aid Scheme and Eco changed in one amendment, submitted, recorded in the
  #               history today, all three flipped; reset in one submit, all three back (same herd, fresh search)
  #   SECTION 4 : amendable herd / 2024 - MSSM and RCSM cards (shown on 2024 only); selected and deselected: as they were
  #   SECTION 5 : two more amendable herds / 2024 - MSSM and RCSM report a state (legacy only opened them)
  #   SECTION 6 : inactive herd (TestData column InactiveHerd) - all ten schemes report a state
  #
  # What was merged (legacy -> here):
  #   - Select-then-deselect was done three times (CRISS, Protein with Next / Back, MSSM / RCSM). It is now one CRISS +
  #     Protein Aid Scheme pass through Next / Back (Section 2) and one MSSM / RCSM pass on 2024 (Section 4).
  #     The selection is now checked as flipped after the click, before it is undone (legacy never checked it).
  #   - Change, submit, check and reset was done twice (CRISS + Protein, then Eco; BISSAGL-7582 AT-TC-04 and 05 were the
  #     same clicks). It is now one amendment with all three schemes and one reset: 2 submits instead of 4.
  #   - Section 3 starts on the screen Section 2 leaves (back at the noted state), so the amendment is not searched for
  #     again; the states noted in Section 2 are the ones Section 3 checks against.
  #   - "the selection state should be readable" on the 2026 herd is covered by "notes the selection state" (it fails when a
  #     card shows no state), so it is not repeated before a change.
  #   - One staff login, and the 2026 amendment is searched for twice instead of 7 times.
  #   - The MSSM / RCSM card text uses the same card table as BISS / CRISS (blank position = found by acronym).
  #
  # Protein Aid Scheme: when Submit Changes reports that the Protein Scheme has no eligible crop, the submit step clicks
  # OK, gives the first tillage parcel the crop staff.protein.crop (Beans - Spring) and submits again; the reset submit
  # puts that parcel's old Parcel Use back first (StaffSteps 21-10-2026).
  #
  # Test data (23-10-2026 - was fixed herds in legacy and in the 22-10-2026 version):
  #   Sections 1 to 5 : "the next amendable herd" - DBRouter "Get Amendable Submitted Herds" (StaffTestData AMENDABLE):
  #                     submitted, no admin check, no Draft / Helpdesk / Draft Dept application, no amendment, two or
  #                     more land parcels, random order. One pool per scheme year. A herd whose search shows no Amend
  #                     link is skipped and the next one tried (staff.amendable.tries, default 5).
  #                     The 2026 herd is amended and reset, so it is left as it was found.
  #   Section 6       : TD:InactiveHerd - the inactive herd comes from the TestData row of TC_12_STAFF (column
  #                     InactiveHerd), so no herd number is written in this file. No query finds inactive herds yet.
  #   Login agr4442 (BISS Co-ordination 1). Password: TD:Password from the TestData row of this test case.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps (Scheme selection and amendments, History)
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Background:
    Given the staff user is logged in to the BISS internal portal as "agr4442"

  @regression @staff @scheme-selection @e2e
